>Out of the six wraiths, not a single one gave me a corpse. 

  Wraiths are much less likely to leave a corpse when killed
by the player on a graveyard level.  The VotD counts as a 
graveyard level, as does the Castle, and I think Orcus and
Moloch's Sanctum.

  Any level where wraiths are summoned (summoned, *not* 
reverse-geno'd) becomes a graveyard level if it isn't already.

  If you want to get corpses from wraiths that are on a graveyard
level, you need to lead them off the level before killing them
yourself.  Luckily, wraiths will follow you up/down stairs.

  Now you know why the path to the VotD downstairs is so twisty
and trapped: to make it tougher to lead wraiths downstairs.

  That's also why the Castle is considered a graveyard level: so
wraiths led up from the VotD have to be led up yet another level
before they're more likely to leave a corpse when killed by the
player.


  The "killed by the player" is important.  Purple worms 
swallowing wraiths whole gain a lot of levels in the VotD.
Non-eating pets killing wraiths can leave corpses for you.
(Conflict might also work.)

