  Yes, I know you're neutral.  If your wizard is non-human, you 
can use the soldiers as sacrifodder.  But even if you can't lead 
the soldiers to the altar as sacrifodder, you can still use the 
zoo monsters for that.  

  Leading the soldiers to the altar will still get all their 
lovely equipment there for curse/enchantment testing.  And 
soldiers tend to have magic-friendly gear:  Gloves, high boots, 
small shields, etc.  

  Even their helms can be useful with other, more spell friendly,
armor.  If you find multiple high-enchantment items of the same
type, consider wearing the second-best until you can foo-proof
the best.

